  "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the damaged items, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of containers is $10+8+6+4+2=30,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{10}{30} \\\\ P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{8}{30} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{6}{30} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{4}{30} \\\\ P(X=4)=f(4) & =\\frac{2}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{10}{30}$ | $\\frac{8}{30}$ | $\\frac{6}{30}$ | $\\frac{4}{30}$ | $\\frac{2}{30}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{10}{30})+1(\\frac{8}{30})+2(\\frac{6}{30})+3(\\frac{4}{30})+4(\\frac{2}{30}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{30}+\\frac{12}{30}+\\frac{12}{30}+\\frac{8}{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
